# Settings that point the site at a Supabase project.
#
# On your own computer: copy this file to .env.local and fill in both values.
# .env.local is ignored by git. Without it, `npm run dev` runs in demo mode with
# sample content.
#
# For the live site: the same two values go in .env.production, which is
# committed on purpose. Both values are public (see below), and the deploy
# workflow reads them from there.

# The project URL, for example https://abcdefghijklmnopqrst.supabase.co
# Supabase dashboard: open the Connect dialog and copy "Project URL".
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The PUBLISHABLE key. It starts with sb_publishable_. On older projects it is
# called the "anon" key instead and starts with eyJ.
# Supabase dashboard: Settings > API Keys > "Publishable key".
#
# This key is meant to be public. It is built into the JavaScript that every
# visitor downloads, and all it allows is what the rules in supabase/schema.sql
# allow: reading trips and published days.
#
# NEVER put the SECRET key here. That is the one that starts with sb_secret_,
# or is labelled "service_role" on older projects. It skips every rule in the
# database, so anyone who saw it could rewrite or delete everything. It does
# not belong in this file, in .env.production, or anywhere else in this
# repository. Nothing in this project needs it.
VITE_SUPABASE_KEY=
